{# With the theme "sistema" the server cannot know the colour scheme of the device, so it renders the light theme and this
   script, before anything is painted, switches to dark when the device asks for it, and follows it afterwards. It acts
   only while the page says "sistema" (the attribute, never the cookie, which the script cannot read), so it is always
   there. A script policy (CSP) would need a hash or a nonce for it, and for the <noscript> style of the layout. The tests
   run this very file (assets/behaviours/theme-inline-script.test.ts): keep the one <script> and no Twig inside it. #}
<script>(() => { const root = document.documentElement; const query = matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)'); const apply = () => { if (root.dataset.jusTema === 'sistema') root.dataset.bsTheme = query.matches ? 'dark' : 'light'; }; apply(); query.addEventListener('change', apply); })();</script>
